- **Web Scraping**
    
    Realm’s web-scraper can be used to scrape any publicly accessible website.
    
    ### Setting up the connection
    
    1. Navigate to Connectors page in Realm
    2. Find “Web Scraping” and click “Manage” and then “+ Add site”
    3. Insert the URL you wish to sync
    4. If you wish to sync only certain URLs, you can add include or exclude patterns to control what parts of your website is synced.
        
        ![Screenshot 2025-04-30 at 11.15.40.png](Realm%20Help%20Center/Screenshot_2025-04-30_at_11.15.40.png)
        
    5. Click Save
- **A connector has failed to sync, what should I do?**
    
    If you notice that a sync of some knowledge has Failed, or hasn’t completed for multiple days, please reach out to the Realm team. Sync issues almost always require some action on our end.
    
    Our team proactively monitors your syncs, but, sometimes, we may have failed to notice a particular failed sync.
    

# Filling RFP/RFIs

- **How do I use Realm to fill out an RFP/RFIs**
    
    Realm can be used to fill out RFPs, RFIs and other information request from customers. The file has to be a spreadsheet (xlsx, xls or csv).
    
    After an initial AI-generated draft, you will also have the opportunity to finalize the RFP together with your team. You can edit the AI-generated answers and assign answers for colleagues to review.
    
    ## Using Realm to fill an RFP/RFI
    
    [RFP workflow.mp4](Realm%20Help%20Center/RFP_workflow.mp4)
    
    ### Filling an RFP
    
    - Make sure you have an **unfilled** version of the RFP on your laptop.
    - Go to “RFPs” in Realm’s main menu.
    - Click “Upload RFP” and upload your RFP.
    - Wait for the file to be parse and analyzed.
    - Review the AI-generated plan for filling each section of the RFP and make edits if necessary. If the plan looks off, you can:
        - Edit the cells, rows and columns to be filled in. Just click on them.
        - Add columns or rows to the section.
        - Skip an entire section. This means that it won’t be filled in with AI.
        - **NB!** The RFP will be broken down into sections that may not correspond to the sheets in the original spreadsheet. This is a feature, not a bug. When you export the final RFP, the spreadsheet will still look exactly like it did originally.
    - Select which Assistant should be used to fill each section. Generally, you should either use Realm (which draws on your company’s whole knowledge base) or a more curated RFP Assistant that your team has created.
    - Hit Fill Section (you’ll need to separately do so for each section). The section will be filled in with your chosen Assistant.
    
    ### Finalizing the RFP together with your team
    
    - Review every AI-generated answer, and do one of the following:
        - Approve the answer (if it’s correct and final)
        - Edit the answer manually
        - Write a follow-up prompt, asking for edits, specification or additions to the answer.
        - Assign the answer for a colleague to review. This will send them an email and a notification in Slack.
    - Ensure that every answer in the RFP is reviewed and approved by you or a colleague.
    - Once all answers have been approved, export the RFP, give it a final check, and send it across to the customer.
- **Are completed RFPs added to my knowledge base?**
    
    Yes! Once you’ve approved all rows of an RFP, it’s marked at “Completed”.
    
    Completed RFPs are automatically added to your knowledge base under a source called “RFPs”. They will automatically become part of the knowledge that Realm draws on.
    
    If the “RFPs” source has been added to the knowledge base of a particular Assistant, that Assistant will also automatically search any completed RFPs.
    
    You can also more specifically curate which RFPs, or which sections of an RFP, are added to a given Assistant.
    
- **How should an RFP be formatted before I upload it to Realm?**
    
    Generally, Realm is designed to handle RFPs with diverse and complicated structures. Most of the time, you won’t need to edit the RFP before uploading it to Realm.
    
    However, if you run into a situation where the RFP looks off after being uploaded to Realm, it might be that you need to simplify the RFP and upload it again. Here are some tips:
    
    - Make sure the question and answer columns form one continuous table. Remove any empty columns that break up the structure.
    - Remove any unnecessary information from the RFP. For example, there might be some additional information outside of the actual area to be answered.
    - Make sure each of the columns that should be answered have descriptive headers, such as “Answer” or “Vendor Answer”.
    - Unmerge any merged cells.

# API

- **What can Realm’s API be used for?**
    
    On a high level, Realm’s API can be used for two things:
    
    1. Push knowledge to Realm from sources that we don’t have a connector for.
    2. Embed a particular Assistant somewhere else, such as inside your own product or help center. This enables use cases like exposing a version of Realm (with access to appropriately curated data) to your own end users.
- **Where can I find documentation for the API?**
    
    The API has its own separate documentation, accessible under “API docs” in the product. Read those for further instructions on how to use the API.
    
